---
import Marketing from '@layouts/Marketing.astro';

// Raw markup, lifted verbatim from the page this replaces.
const body = `<div class="shell">
  <section class="band doc" style="border-top:none">
<h2>Support</h2>

<h3>Get in touch</h3>
<p class="txt">Questions, bug reports and feature requests all go to the same place, and
the address opens with the App Store listing.
<!-- BLOCKER: App Store Connect requires a working support URL and contact at
     submission. Put the real address here before submitting; the previous
     placeholder (support@moshpit.example) was a live mailto to a domain that
     does not exist, which is worse than saying nothing. --></p>

<h3>Common questions</h3>

<h4>Does Moshpit need anything installed on my server?</h4>
<p class="txt">No. It's a standard SSH client out of the box. <code>mosh</code>,
<code>tmux</code> and <code>herdr</code> are each optional — if one is missing,
Moshpit tells you and offers the install command; it never installs anything
silently and never falls back to a different multiplexer behind your back.</p>

<h4>How does agent status work?</h4>
<p class="txt">On <code>herdr</code>, agent state is part of the protocol — zero setup.
On <code>tmux</code>, a one-line hook install (offered in Settings) lets
Claude Code and friends report state; without it, Moshpit falls back to
output heuristics.</p>

<h4>Why does iOS ask for Local Network permission?</h4>
<p class="txt">Only so SSH/Mosh can reach hosts on your own LAN (192.168.x.x and similar).
Deny it and internet hosts still work fine.</p>

<h4>Is my data collected?</h4>
<p class="txt">No — nothing is. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>;
the App Store label is <em>Data Not Collected</em>.</p>
  </section>
</div>`;
---

<Marketing
  title="Support — Moshpit"
  description="How to reach us, and answers to the questions that come up most often."
  path="support"
  lang="en"
  translated={false}
>
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
</Marketing>
